    "description": "•\tSoftware Technical Lead/Architect/Subject Matter Expert for rapidly growing suite of products: \no\tGround Station - Cloud hosted application to that acts serves as the landing zone and remote management interface for devices installed on aircraft to synchronize data with.  Includes Web-frontend to provide remote status and control of IoT devices in the field (AID).  A REST API is provided for interacting with the IoT devices to exchange data. \no\tAircraft Interface Device (AID) - Custom built data collection and processing unit installed within an aircraft running an embedded Linux distribution.  Includes multiple hosted applications for collection and conversion of aircraft data and status information that can be uploaded to the Ground Station for further analysis.\n•\tOversaw teams of 4-12 on-site software engineers in addition to offshore test/design team\n•\tSuccessfully led teams through software design, verification, transition to manufacturing and field support of several products, including complex systems involving multiple products\n•\tLed initiative to secure/harden devices to permit autonomous internet connections, including successful 3rd party security scans/audits\n•\tFostered a Continuous Integration culture by creating automated build and test pipelines to reduce recurring manual test effort and provide quick feedback of changes\n•\tContributed to numerous bid and proposal activities, as well as preparation of live demonstrations for customer visits, trade shows and internal executive leadership\n•\tPrepared and presented numerous design reviews (customers, engineering management, chief engineers, hardware engineers, systems engineers, etc.)\n•\tMentored and trained junior engineers and interns, and cross trained senior engineers",
